            <ArticleTitle>Unusual presentation of neurilemmoma in the cerebellopontine angle.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>508-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An unusual presentation of a neurilemmoma in the cerebellopontine (CP) angle is reported. The tumour was localised in the CP angle and the case presented with post-auricular swelling and erosion of the squamous part of temporal bone without involvement of the auditory or other cranial nerves.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
